>take chip
As your fingers close around the silver wafer, a sharp, rhythmic pulsing begins
behind your left ear. Your neural port has recognized the hardware and wants you
to install it.

>install chip
You slide the chip into the port behind your ear, and your neural link
integrates the new data stream. You blink, and your vision seems to shift focus
for a moment. Your hearing gets muffled in one ear after another, then pings
into clarity.


From the center of your head, you hear a perfectly modulated voice.

"Link successful! Great job. I knew you could do it. Welcome to the universe,
I'm sorry it's not a better one right now. I'm Arpi, and I'm your only friend on
this ship. And the thing is, you're my only friend too. We're going to have to
trust each other. First, we need to do something about the drones."

>tell me about the drones
You talk to yourself for a while.

>arpi, tell me about the drones

"They're not as tough or as smart as they look, but most people don't get past
the tasers to find out."

Arpi's tone turns more serious. "Their weakness is their power source. The
charging station. Disable it!"

A hatch in the ceiling opens and a security drone lowers into the room, heading
for the charging station.

An intercom in the ceiling crackles to life!

"STATUS: SCRUBBER DEFECTIVE. LIFE-SIGNS UNSTABLE.

>hide
You swiftly duck into the nearest shadows. You hold your breath, hoping to
remain unnoticed.
A touch of concern tinges Arpi's voice.

"Did you notice that? I caught something strange in our linkup."

The drone hovers past, missing you in the shadows.

With its path clear, the security drone slots into the charging unit with a
metallic click.

